-- One-time data migration (2026-11-11): University Admission wording and the ready-made preparation directions. No schema change.
--
-- Brings the site settings to packages/shared/src/university-packages.ts and sample-data.ts, on top of 20261110:
--   * homepage section: the title and description become "Oliy ta’limga kiriş" / "Поступление в вузы" / "University Admission"
--     and the new description, each only while it is still the text 20261106 wrote;
--   * directions: General, IT & Engineering and Economics & Business are added when missing; Medicine and Law get their
--     shorter names, only while they are still exactly what 20261110 wrote;
--   * packages: the seven packages of the three new directions are added when missing, each subject mapped to this tenant's
--     offline course by id, else by slug (a subject without such a course stays listed as not covered, never a made-up
--     course), and published by the rule of presetPublishability, as in 20261110. Unverified requirements are published
--     marked "requires confirmation" on the site. Prices are not stored.
--
-- Guarded: anything an admin changed since is skipped and reported, nothing is removed, and a package that already exists is
-- never replaced. No other setting, user, subscription, payment, enrollment, course or group is touched.
-- Safety: the stored universities, packages, homepage section and version are written to "AuditEvent" (action 'content.sync',
-- id 'university-admission-20261111-SiteConfig') first; the update runs in its own sub-transaction, so a failure is rolled
-- back and reported without failing the migration. A database without the ILMORA catalog (tests, fresh installs) is left
-- untouched, and running it again changes nothing.
-- Undo: set "SiteConfig".data->'universities', ->'presets' and the homepage section back to the "before" values of that audit row.

DO $sync$
